README.md:11:The web chat (and the CLI) talk to the **Assistant**, the primary orchestrator, or directly to any specialist agent. It handles general conversation directly and delegates company and market research to the **Market Researcher**, which owns the Crustdata company search, enrichment, and web search tools. Business financial analysis goes to the **CFO Agent**, which analyzes figures supplied in the conversation, including cash flow, runway, budgets, pricing, and hiring scenarios. For combined requests, the Assistant passes market research findings to the CFO Agent and synthesizes the final reply. GitHub questions (repositories, issues, pull requests, Actions runs) go to a read-only copy of the **GitHub Agent**, and questions about past agent runs (failures, latency, token usage, detections, triage) go to a read-only copy of the **Neatlogs Agent**.
README.md:15:The **GitHub Agent** connects to GitHub's official remote MCP server (repos, issues, pull requests, Actions, account context) using `GITHUB_PAT`. In the web chat it can also make changes, but every tool the server does not mark read-only (`readOnlyHint: true`) pauses for an inline Approve/Deny card; a denied call never runs, and sending a new message drops any approval left unanswered. The Assistant only ever gets its read-only tools, so it cannot write to GitHub. Without `GITHUB_PAT` the agent starts with no tools.
README.md:23:Copy `.env.example` to `.env` and fill in the provider and integration credentials. For the GitHub Agent, set `GITHUB_PAT` to a fine-grained personal access token scoped to the repositories it may use (read/write on Contents, Issues, Pull requests and Actions for changes; read-only permissions are enough for inspection).
README.md:36:- **Neatlogs MCP**: The Neatlogs Agent uses Neatlogs' hosted MCP server (`https://ingest.neatlogs.com/mcp`) through `@mastra/mcp`, authenticated with the existing `NEATLOGS_API_KEY`. Tools are gated by name (the server sends no read-only annotations): reads run directly, writes and unknown tools need approval.
